  "acrm---key-feature-1-content": "<h3>Orders read from email and PDF</h3><p>Customer POs sent as PDF attachments or typed into an email become a draft sales order with the customer, lines, quantities, prices, and ship-to. Unclear fields go to a person.</p>",
  "acrm---key-feature-4-content": "<h3>Stock reserved when an order is released</h3><p>Released lines reserve stock on hand. A short line ships what is there and backorders the rest, and the warehouse works from one pick list built from the day's released orders.</p>",
  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Order Processing Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is order processing automation?\", \"a\": \"Order processing automation is software that carries a customer order from the moment it arrives until it is released to the warehouse, running the checks a person would otherwise run by hand. Clean orders go straight through. Your team only sees the orders that break a rule, such as a wrong price or a customer past their limit.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I set up order processing automation?\", \"a\": \"Write down where orders arrive and which ones your desk stops today, then describe both in plain English to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-automation-builder'>AI automation builder</a>. Emergent builds the workflow and the database behind it. Connect your ERP through its API so released orders land where your accounting team expects them, and change any rule later by prompting.\"}, {\"q\": \"What order data do I need before building order processing automation?\", \"a\": \"Start with your catalog and its part numbers, then the price and credit tables the checks will read. Add a cross-reference for customers who order by their own part numbers, since a PO line reading HH-DS22 has to map to your SKU. Emergent sets no task cap on the workflows it builds, however many orders arrive in a day.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should happen to an order that fails a price or credit check?\", \"a\": \"Hold the order at the step that failed and send it to the one person who owns that decision, with the reason attached. A price mismatch goes to the account rep; an account over its limit goes to credit. The buyer can still get a receipt that the order arrived, and that email is the work of <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-automation-builder/order-confirmation'>order confirmation automation</a>, not of the hold.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can order processing automation read emailed orders into sales orders?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Point the app at the inbox where customers send orders, and it reads each attachment into fields with AI: customer, PO number, part numbers, quantities, and prices. Any field it reads with low confidence goes to a person before the sales order is drafted. Track how often the desk corrects a field during the first month, account by account.\"}, {\"q\": \"How does order processing handle a customer who sends the same order twice?\", \"a\": \"The app looks up the customer's PO number before it drafts a sales order. If that number already sits on an open order, the second email is parked for the desk with a link to the first, and nothing new reaches the warehouse. A person then decides whether it is a resend or a genuine change to quantities.\"}, {\"q\": \"What does automated order management cover after an order is entered?\", \"a\": \"It covers everything after entry, up to the status a buyer sees when they check on it. Automated order management keeps one record per order that every step writes to. The warehouse and customer service then read one status from it. Reorder points and stock counts sit with <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-automation-builder/automated-inventory-management'>automated inventory management</a>, which feeds the stock check.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should an automated order management system connect to?\", \"a\": \"At minimum, it should connect to the system that holds your inventory and invoices, such as your ERP. An automated order management system that cannot read stock levels will promise lines it cannot ship. Built on Emergent, the app connects to any tool with an API and keeps the records in sync in both directions.\"}, {\"q\": \"When is order management automation worth building?\", \"a\": \"Build it when your desk spends its day retyping the same fields from emails into the ERP, and when holds get lost in someone's inbox. A shop keying a handful of orders a week can stay manual. Emergent builds order management automation from a plain-English description of the rules your desk already follows.\"}, {\"q\": \"How is order fulfillment automation different from order processing?\", \"a\": \"Order processing ends when an order is checked and released, and order fulfillment automation picks up from there with picking and packing. Both read one order record, which is how a buyer sees tracking on the order they placed. Buying stock from suppliers to cover a backorder is a separate job, handled by <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-automation-builder/procurement'>procurement automation</a>.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 }
